op_ut,third_party.torch-xpu-ops.test.xpu.dynamo.test_streams_xpu.TestStreams,test_nested_stream_enter_exit
op_ut,third_party.torch-xpu-ops.test.xpu.dynamo.test_streams_xpu.TestStreams,test_epilogue_copy_streams_inference
op_ut,third_party.torch-xpu-ops.test.xpu.dynamo.test_streams_xpu.TestStreams,test_epilogue_copy_stream_tracking
op_ut,third_party.torch-xpu-ops.test.xpu.dynamo.test_streams_xpu.TestStreams,test_event_tracing
~~op_ut,third_party.torch-xpu-ops.test.xpu.dynamo.test_compiler_bisector_xpu.TestCompilerBisector,test_pre_grad~~
~~op_ut,third_party.torch-xpu-ops.test.xpu.dynamo.test_wrap_inductor_compiled_regions_xpu.TestWrapInductorCompiledRegions,test_wrap_config_affects_cache_key~~

### Context
Surfaced while reviewing CI for torch-xpu-ops PR #3383
(https://github.com/intel/torch-xpu-ops/pull/3383, run 25042442065). All
files above are added/modified by that PR.

### Failure summary

#### A. `Torch not compiled with CUDA enabled` (2 cases)
- `test_record_stream_problem_basic`
- `test_record_stream_problem_interleaved`

The test bodies in `test/xpu/dynamo/test_streams_xpu.py` unconditionally
hit `torch.cuda.*` (or call `record_stream` on a CUDA tensor). They need
to be ported to use `torch.xpu.*`. **This is a port bug, not a torch
upstream bug.** Fix in PR #3383.

NOTE: an existing `Known_issue.log` entry uses single-comma form
`op_ut,...test_streams_xpu,TestStreams.test_record_stream_problem_basic_xpu`
with `_xpu` suffix; the runner now emits two-comma form
`op_ut,...test_streams_xpu.TestStreams,test_record_stream_problem_basic`
without `_xpu` suffix. The pre-existing tracker needs its `Cases:` lines
updated to the new format.

#### B. Output-graph stream-id text mismatch (11 cases)
Tests that compare a generated FX graph against an expected string fail
because the assigned stream id differs by 1 on XPU vs CUDA. Example diff:
```
'stream': 0  vs  'stream': 1
```

This indicates the XPU stream-tracking dynamo pass numbers streams
differently (or the default-stream counter on XPU starts at a different
index). Either the port should regenerate expected outputs against XPU,
or the dynamo stream-id allocation needs to be deterministic across
backends.

#### C. Recompile-counter mismatch (2 cases)
- `dynamo/test_compiler_bisector_xpu.py::TestCompilerBisector::test_pre_grad` — `AssertionError: Scalars are not equal!`
- `dynamo/test_wrap_inductor_compiled_regions_xpu.py::TestWrapInductorCompiledRegions::test_wrap_config_affects_cache_key` — `AssertionError: Scalars are not equal!`

Same family as Bucket C cases #2 — XPU compile pipeline produces a
different `frame_count` than expected.

### Reproducer
```
cd third_party/torch-xpu-ops/test/xpu
pytest -v dynamo/test_streams_xpu.py::TestStreams::test_record_stream_problem_basic
pytest -v dynamo/test_streams_xpu.py::TestStreams::test_stream_enter_exit
pytest -v dynamo/test_compiler_bisector_xpu.py::TestCompilerBisector::test_pre_grad
```

### Versions
- torch nightly XPU 2.13.0.dev20260422+xpu (per CI)
- torch-xpu-ops PR #3383 head




