Issue #3388: [Bug Skip] XPU Dynamo Graph Lowering - stream_index None
<!-- agent:status:IN_REVIEW -->

## Summary
CUDA-specific stream APIs fail under torch.compile with Dynamo graph lowering because streams::wait_stream/record_event operators expect explicit stream_index but receive None.

## Test Info
- **Test Type:** ut
- **Category:** dynamo
- **Dependency:** 
- **Platform:** XPU

## Failed Tests
- `third_party/torch-xpu-ops/test/xpu/dynamo/test_ctx_manager_xpu.py::CtxManagerTests::test_cuda_event_method`

## Error Log
```
File "torch/_dynamo/eval_frame.py", line 1281, in _fn
    return fn(*args, **kwargs)
  File "<eval_with_key>.1298", line 11, in forward
    record_event = torch.ops.streams.record_event(1, None)
RuntimeError: streams::record_event() Expected a value of type int for argument stream_index but instead found type NoneType.
```

## Reproducer
```bash
cd ~/daisy_pytorch/third_party/torch-xpu-ops/test/xpu && pytest -v dynamo/test_ctx_manager_xpu.py -k test_cuda_event_method
```

## Commit Scope


## Root Cause Analysis
In torch/_dynamo/variables/builder.py wrap_fx_proxy_cls (line 3547-3559), when a StreamVariable is created from a proxy whose target is device_interface.current_stream rather than get_external_object_by_index, user_object_index is set to None. Subsequently, when record_event() or wait_event() is called on this StreamVariable, None is passed as stream_index to torch.ops.streams.record_event/wait_stream, causing the RuntimeError since those ops require an int.

## Proposed Fix Strategy
In builder.py wrap_fx_proxy_cls, for the device_interface.current_stream proxy target branch, look up or register the stream in the user object table and set user_object_index accordingly (similar to how register_user_object is called in builder.py:1225). Also check that torch.xpu.Stream() construction in user_defined.py:1349-1374 returns a StreamVariable (with user_object_index=ind) rather than a plain wrap_fx_proxy TensorVariable, so wait_event/record_event can be dispatched to StreamVariable.call_method.

