  File "torch/_dynamo/eval_frame.py", line 1281, in _fn
    return fn(*args, **kwargs)
  File "<eval_with_key>.1298", line 11, in forward
    record_event = torch.ops.streams.record_event(1, None)
RuntimeError: streams::record_event() Expected a value of type int for argument stream_index but instead found type NoneType.
```

## Root Cause

Dynamo traces torch.xpu.Stream.wait_stream but lowers to primitive streams::wait_stream() op expecting explicit int for stream_index but receives None.

## Related PyTorch Issues

- pytorch#180179 - torch.cuda.Stream traced incorrectly by torch.compile
- pytorch#178155 (DISABLED) - test_cuda_event_record_on_stream failing
- pytorch#134746 (DISABLED) - test_record_stream flaky
- pytorch#138557 (DISABLED) - test_record_stream_cuda_float32

