  **Fix Strategy:** Investigate whether FakeTensorMode or XPU-specific dispatch is creating weakrefs on tensors during .to() conversion. The fix likely belongs in torch/_subclasses/fake_tensor.py or the XPU backend's tensor creation path. Alternatively, swap_tensors in torch/utils/__init__.py could be updated to clear weakrefs on t2 before swapping (since t2 is the newly created tensor and its weakrefs are transient). Another option: check if nn/modules/module.py _apply() should handle this case more gracefully.

  **Tokens:** model: claude-sonnet-4 | tokens: 177.4K | in: 10 | out: 2.1K | cache_read: 167.0K | cache_write: 8.2K | cost: $0.1120
  Log: `agent-issue-2712-triaging-20260517-190042.log`
