## Reproducer
```bash
PYTORCH_TEST_WITH_SLOW=1 pytest -v test/test_ops_gradients.py -k test_inplace_gradgrad_index_reduce_prod_xpu_float64
```

## Commit Scope


## Root Cause Analysis
The XPU index_reduce kernel explicitly calls `globalContext().alertNotDeterministic("index_reduce_xpu")` (Indexing.cpp:1417), meaning the kernel is intentionally non-deterministic. The gradgradcheck reentrancy test runs backward twice with identical inputs and expects bit-identical results, but the non-deterministic scatter-based reduction in the backward pass produces different values each run, triggering the GradcheckError.

## Proposed Fix Strategy
Implement a deterministic path in index_reduce_func_xpu_template (src/ATen/native/xpu/sycl/Indexing.cpp) that is used when torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True) or gradcheck's determinism check is active. This may involve serializing the atomic scatter operations or using a sort-then-reduce approach. Alternatively, if the backward formula itself is non-deterministic, fix the backward kernel (index_reduce_backward on XPU) similarly. The alertNotDeterministic call should remain but the kernel should also provide a deterministic fallback.

## Target Repository
torch-xpu-ops


