**Proposed Fix Strategy:** Implement a deterministic path in index_reduce_func_xpu_template (src/ATen/native/xpu/sycl/Indexing.cpp) that is used when torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True) or gradcheck's determinism check is active. This may involve serializing the atomic scatter operations or using a sort-then-reduce approach. Alternatively, if the backward formula itself is non-deterministic, fix the backward kernel (index_reduce_backward on XPU) similarly. The alertNotDeterministic call should remain but the kernel should also provide a deterministic fallback.

